# TRET.AI project rules

- Build ONLY what the current version prompt lists. Do not start any later module. No placeholder pages, no unused code, no speculative features.
- If something is unclear, do NOT guess. Write it as OPEN in docs/decisions.md and continue with the rest. Ask only if completely blocked.
- TypeScript strict. Money is never a float. (No money code exists yet; keep this rule for later.)
- Secrets never go in the repo. Provide .env.example with variable names only.
- Every table has Row Level Security. Dev data only: no real Legacy data in this database until the owner says so.
- All LLM calls, when added later, go through one module called llm-gateway. Do not create it until that module is in scope.
- Every change ends with: updated docs, updated CHANGELOG.md, VERSION bumped only when the owner says, a short commit message in the form "v0.0.0.1: <what changed>" (adjust the version prefix to match VERSION when bumped).
- Work on branch build/v0.0.0.1 (or the matching build branch) and open a pull request into main. Do not push directly to main.
- App version source of truth is the VERSION file only. package.json version stays 0.0.0 because npm cannot hold 4-part versions.
